  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#origin-2\n\n> If A and B are the same opaque origin, then return true.\n\nThis is in conflict with what the URL specification states about opaque origins:\n\nhttps://url.spec.whatwg.org/#origin\n\n> Otherwise\n> Return a new opaque origin.\n> **This does indeed mean that these URLs cannot be same-origin with themselves.**\n\nAs far as I understand and read this as that when you have an origin of `null` (which is the opaque origin string) it cannot be `same-origin` as the origin cannot be determined. \n\nSo the specification should be altered to\n\n> If A and B are the same opaque origin, then return **false**.\n",
